## Arrays: cast and reshape

Casting can be used to change the datatype of an array or its shape, as shown in the example.

Reshaping or casting a scalar into an array creates an array filled with that scalar value. For example, `[2][2]float32(5)` returns an array of `float32` and axis lengths `[2][2]` initialized with 5. Note the use of `()` as in a cast instead of `{}`.
